it's 11:00 a.m. at the Rio Club Hotel  Resort on Gran Canaria for the last hour  professional host Yuri slay lay out  Gonzalez has been putting a group of  vacationers through their paces after  some stretching she moves on to a  30-minute aqua aerobics session  Yuriy as her friends caller was born in  Cuba she's lived on Gran Canaria for  seven years she works at the 4-star  resort five days a week  he Agathe caviar my work is all about  energizing the guests I'm constantly  talking to people and I like to convey  urge what have you that's the most  important thing positive energy and good  vibes not everyone can do that you have  to be a certain type to do this kind of  work locally in the West this sort of  hotel tends to attract families the team  of hosts is a big draw for them many  people booked a stay here because of the  wide range of activities  the resort is in mass Palomas one of the  most popular destinations on the island  tourism is Gran Canaria is most  important industry Yuri has worked here  for three years now  one of her main duties is maintaining a  good relationship with guests this hotel  is just perfect we've been coming here  for 13 years every year we come here and  we just feel great at 12:30 it's time  for the rehearsal for the evening  performance along with speaking several  languages and being physically fit the  job requires acting and dancing talent  too as a trained dancer that part comes  naturally to Yuri but it still took her  a while to grow into the job when you  start out the job can be stressful you  think oh god I have to do this then I  have to run to the next thing  but once you get used to it and have fun  with it it's no problem you find a  rhythm you prepare activities leave them  eat lunch go home do the evening show  then it starts all over again after the  rehearsal the team meets to discuss the  upcoming activities there are 17 hosts  working here  today the activities director of the  hotel chain is here as well  Gerhardt Cotswolds from Austria he's  responsible for recruiting and training  the team and knows exactly what sort of  people he's looking for they can't be  shy  they have to be friendly and talented  when it comes to our evening shows they  can't be nervous on stage or with the  microphone in their hand they need to be  outgoing at 3 o'clock the team gives a  small performance by the pool and lets  the guests know what activities are  planned for the afternoon before URI  leads her next activity she shows us  what some of her colleagues are up to  while Maria from Spain is doing strength  training Nena from Germany is in the  hotel's art studio helping guests get in  touch with their creativity  a few meters away a Dutch colleague is  doing the same but with younger guests  at 3:30 Yuri's working again this time  giving a salsa class Yuri lives off-site  she's also a mother which doesn't leave  her much time for herself  boy when I go on holiday I go somewhere  where there are no people then I can  have time and space for myself somewhere  quiet where I can relax with no stress  of course I love partying and excitement  but that's not what I'm looking for in  my own holiday : idealist  Yuri eats dinner at home then she's back  at the resort at 8:30 in time to prepare  for the evening performance  yeah that a lot huh I do get tired after  a typical day of classes looking after  the guests and generally having a lot to  do but at the same time I still have  energy and I look forward to the  performances I love my job so it never  feels like a chore  tomorrow at 10 o'clock it all starts  again URI will be back making sure the  guests have a holiday to remember
 

